*** GAMS/LINDO option file for ReEDS
*** Docs: https://www.gams.com/latest/docs/S_LINDO.html
*** Activate with: model.OptFile = 1;
***
*** NOTE: every option below previously used LINDO-API-style names
*** (LS_IPARAM_*/LS_DPARAM_*). Those are C API constants, not GAMS
*** option-file identifiers, so GAMS/LINDO rejected all of them at
*** solve time ("Unknown option ...") and silently ran on defaults
*** the whole time. The real GAMS/LINDO option names (from
*** optlindo.def / S_LINDO.html) are used below instead.
***
*** NOTE: this GAMS/LINDO license does not include the Barrier solver
*** (that needs a separate GAMS/MOSEK barrier license). Every prior
*** LINDO solve log confirms this - "Barrier Solver Version 0.0.000" -
*** and LINDO automatically falls back to dual simplex. So this file
*** asks for dual simplex explicitly rather than an unusable
*** barrier+crossover method.

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Algorithm selection
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** SOLVER_METHOD: 0 free (auto), 1 primal simplex, 2 dual simplex,
***                3 barrier (unlicensed here), 4 NLP, 5 MIP, ...
*** Dual simplex gives the basic solution downstream ReEDS code expects,
*** and matches what LINDO already falls back to for this model.
SOLVER_METHOD 2

*** Dual simplex strategy: 0 solver decides, 1 single-phase, 2 two-phase
SPLEX_DUAL_PHASE 1

*** Run barrier and simplex concurrently if at least 2 threads are available.
*** Left OFF: with no licensed barrier solver, "concurrent" just means racing
*** multiple simplex variants against each other, and on this badly-scaled
*** model the threads have been observed to converge to different, mutually
*** inconsistent answers - LINDO then reports overall status "unknown" and
*** GAMS aborts the run.
*** 0 off, 1 on if >= 2 threads, 2 always concurrent
SOLVER_CONCURRENT_OPTMODE 0

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Parallelism
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Both multithreading strategies for the LP solve have failed on this model:
*** - default/concurrent (MULTITHREAD_MODE -1 or left implicit via NUM_THREADS>1):
***   races independent algorithm attempts across threads; they disagree with
***   each other and LINDO reports overall status "unknown".
*** - MULTITHREAD_MODE 2 (parallel-only): hard-fails immediately with
***   "Specified feature is not yet supported or not compatible with the
***   model type" - parallel mode isn't implemented for LP/dual-simplex in
***   this LINDO build.
*** So: run single-threaded. This model is small enough (ERCOT-scale, ~13.5k
*** constraints) that the earlier 8-thread concurrent race only took ~14s
*** total anyway - single-threaded dual simplex should still be fast, and is
*** the only mode that actually returns a correct, deterministic answer.
NUM_THREADS 1

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Time / iteration limits
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** LP time limit in seconds (-1 = no limit). 2 days matches cplex.opt.
SOLVER_TIMLMT 172800

*** Global LP iteration limit (-1 = no limit)
LP_ITRLMT -1

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Tolerances - matched to ReEDS cplex.opt where possible
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Primal feasibility tolerance (CPLEX eprhs 1e-5)
SOLVER_FEASTOL 1e-5

*** Dual feasibility / optimality tolerance (CPLEX epopt 1e-6)
SOLVER_OPTTOL 1e-6

*** Simplex pivot zero tolerance
LP_PIV_ZEROTOL 1e-7

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Pre-processing / scaling
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Scaling: 0 off, 1 on
LP_SCALE 1

*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** Warm start
*** ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*** 1 = use any basis already in memory (warm start), 0 = cold start.
*** ReEDS sequentially advances years, so warm-starting between SOLVEs is helpful
*** when feasible.
SOLVER_RESTART 1

threads=8